Zram (04-config → lib/scripts/zram.sh)
  HyprGruv default (64 GB host, 2026-09-10): cap compressed swap at 8 GiB.
  ram / 2 auto-grows with RAM and is too large above ~16 GB (filling zram
  can eat 8–16 GiB of real RAM for compressed pages).

  /etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf
    [zram0]
    zram-size = min(ram / 2, 8192)
    compression-algorithm = zstd
    swap-priority = 100

  /etc/sysctl.d/99-zram.conf
    vm.page-cluster = 0          # single-page swap; 3 is for disk

  Notes:
    - zswap stays off (kernel cmdline zswap.enabled=0). Do not stack zswap on zram.
    - No disk swap on the live host. Hibernate needs a disk swap file/partition ≥ RAM;
      zram does not survive power-off.
    - Verify: zramctl && swapon --show && sysctl vm.page-cluster
    - Wizard still offers uncapped ram/2, ram/4, and a 4 GiB cap.
